course: dictionary
lesson: 10639
title: Reading the prefix un-
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unhurt means not injured or harmed. The prefix un- means not, so unhurt is hurt with not in front of it, just like unhappy means not happy and unkind means not kind. You often meet it after accidents, falls, crashes and fires.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Toad jumped, rolled down a short embankment, picked himself up unhurt, scrambled into the wood and hid.» He rolled down a bank, so he might have been hurt. Picking himself up and running away shows that he was not.
explain: Notice where unhurt sits in the sentence: it comes after a verb, as in «picked himself up unhurt». To check your meaning, swap in «not hurt». «Picked himself up not hurt» still makes sense, so you have understood it correctly.
fact: Unhurt means not injured or harmed, especially after an accident or danger.
fact: The un- at the start means not, so unhurt is the same as "not hurt".
fact: Unhurt is usually used after a verb, as in «escaped unhurt» or «was found unhurt».
fact: Unhurt tells you that someone was in danger but is now safe.
fact: Other un- words work the same way: unhappy means not happy, and unkind means not kind.
exercise: «He fell off his bike, but he got up unhurt.» What does unhurt mean? | Covered in mud | Very tired | *Not injured | Still riding his bike
exercise: In the word unhurt, what does the un- mean? | Again | Very | Before | *Not
exercise: «The car crashed, but the driver was found unhurt.» Which meaning fits best? | Angry about the crash | Lost and far from the road | *Safe, with no injuries | Asleep in a field
test: Toad «picked himself up unhurt» after rolling down the embankment. What does this tell us? | Toad was rolling down the bank on purpose | Toad was too scared to move | Toad was hurt badly by the fall | *Toad was not injured by the fall
test: Which sentence uses unhurt correctly? | The hikers unhurt reached the camp the storm. | The hikers reached the camp unhurting after the storm. | *The hikers reached the camp unhurt after the storm, having taken shelter in time. | The hikers reached the camp unhurt after the storm.
exam: Ella says unhurt means very hungry. Which answer is right? | *Ella is wrong, because unhurt means not injured or harmed | Ella is right, because the un- means very | Ella is wrong, because unhurt means very happy | Ella is right, because unhurt is a word about food
